<attribute name="version" nodeId="5579dcb"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="4cd9dd85">&lt;p&gt;
    Determine who will be responsible for:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reviewing all&amp;nbsp;change requests&amp;nbsp;forwarded for review
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Considering all supporting documentation
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Approving / rejecting each&amp;nbsp;change request&amp;nbsp;based on its relevant merits
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Resolving change conflict (where 2 or more changes overlap)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identifying the implementation timetable (for approved changes)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Authorize this body to be the principle authority for all change request decision making.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The change control board will determine the feasiblity of change by examining factors, such as:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Risk to the project in implementing the change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Risk to the project in NOT implementing the change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Impact on the project in implementing the change (time, resources, finance, quality).
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    In formal change request reviews, the change control board may:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reject the change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Request more information related to the change
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Approve the change as requested
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Approve the change subject to specified conditions
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Confirm&amp;nbsp;that the change control board has review policy, processes and supporting documentation in place prior to
    project delivery.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="283f4b6a"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="2a9f2c2f"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="440260af"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="c7e37c6e">The primary purpose of this task is to make sure the required change management boards are established to handle the
different types of changes expected on the project.&amp;nbsp; As due diligence it is important to make sure each board has
proper representation from the various interested parties and is authorized to make decisions on any changes submitted.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="cf145309"></attribute>
</Element>
